# terminal-manager-switch: pluggable terminal manager end-to-end (Phase 8 of
# plans/260926-0218-swarm-refactor-terminal-manager).
#
# Multi-agent spawning + terminal injection through the TerminalDriver seam
# (src/terminal/index.ts getTerminalDriver / TmuxDriver / HerdrDriver / MockTerminalDriver).
#
# Pattern 2 (seeded world + single-actor root script) per the mock-llm-scenarios skill:
# the engine (spawn preflight, driver-backed liveness probe, sendKeys injection guard,
# capture-pane driver routing) runs for real on the seeded state; the scripted root turns
# only observe + assert. The lane harness sets PI_SWARM_TERMINAL_MANAGER + TMUX/HERDR env
# so the driver resolution is the thing under test, and asserts:
#   T1  getTerminalDriver() resolves from PI_SWARM_TERMINAL_MANAGER (tmux | herdr | default tmux)
#   T2  spawn: agent record carries driver-appropriate tmuxTarget + tmuxAlive probe result
#   T3  injection: kickoff/identity prompt reaches the pane via driver sendText/sendKeys
#       (root-pane reject guard intact: targets == root's tmuxTarget are refused)
#   T4  capture: capturePane routes through the active driver and persists to traces/tmux/
#   T5  settle: worker acks + task update flow through mailbox delivery as usual
#
# Turn 1 — root inspects driver state + spawns the scripted worker.
# Turn 2 — root injects keys to the worker pane (terminal injection) and verifies capture.
# Turn 3 — root settles after confirming worker ack + mailbox delivery.
